{"conversation_id": "conv_003", "status": "started", "response": "It sounds like you’re in a really painful place right now, and I’m glad you were able to put that into words. Feeling like there’s no point and not being sure you want to keep going can be incredibly heavy and isolating, and it makes sense that you’d be exhausted by that. Your experience matters, and it deserves to be taken seriously.

You don’t have to figure this out alone. If you can, consider reaching out to someone you trust and telling them—honestly and directly—how bad things feel, even if you’re not sure what you need. If you’re open to it, talking with a mental health professional (like a therapist, counselor, or doctor) can give you a space that’s specifically meant for sorting through thoughts like these and helping you stay safe.

If at any point your thoughts about not wanting to go on start turning into plans or urges to hurt yourself, that’s a situation where immediate support really matters. In that case, please contact your local emergency number or a crisis line in your country (for example, many countries have a 24/7 suicide prevention hotline or text/chat service). You deserve support that meets the intensity of what you’re going through.", "tokens_used": {"input": 1517, "output": 254, "cached": 1408}}

